##  Overview
The goal of this project was to compare multiple data structures—**vector**, **hash table**, and **binary search tree (BST)**—to determine which would be the most efficient and practical for storing and retrieving course information in the university advising program.  
The chosen structure would later be implemented in Project Two to display courses in alphanumeric order and support prerequisite lookups.

---

##  Pseudocode Overview

### **Vector**
loadCourses(filename)
open file
for each line in file
parse course data
add course to vector

**Search Function**
findCourse(courseNumber)
for each course in vector
if courseNumber matches
return course
return not found


---

### **Hash Table**
insertCourse(course)
compute hash from courseNumber
find appropriate bucket
place course in bucket

**Search Function**
findCourse(courseNumber)
compute hash from courseNumber
look in bucket for match
return course or not found

---

### **Binary Search Tree (BST)**
insert(node, course)
if node is null
create new node with course
else if courseNumber < node.courseNumber
insert left
else
insert right


**Search Function**
find(node, courseNumber)
if node is null
return not found
else if courseNumber == node.courseNumber
return course
else if courseNumber < node.courseNumber
search left
else
search right


